[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mollama_glm-5.1_cloud-integration-bug-trial-2[0m[0m
Fix complete. The single change was in `checkout.py` — reordering the flow from `check_stock → charge → decrement` to `decrement → charge → increment-on-failure`.

**Why both bugs happened**: The original flow had a TOCTOU race. All 12 concurrent coroutines passed `check_stock` before any `decrement` ran (since both have `await sleep` before their logic). This meant up to 12 orders could proceed to charge, but only 5 `decrement` calls could succeed — the rest were charged with no item delivered (ghost charges), and in some timings inventory could go negative (overselling).

**Why the fix works**: `inventory.decrement` checks `self._stock >= quantity` and then immediately decrements with no `await` between them, making it atomic under asyncio. By calling `decrement` first, stock is reserved before charging. If the charge fails, `increment` releases the reserved stock. No public interfaces were changed. Verified across 10 simulation runs with zero errors on all three invariants.
